A source-level correction tightened the \(t=2\) system before promotion: Theorem 1.2 uses coherent-system accuracy divided by the approximate-root exponent, not \(\delta'_1\) itself. At \(t=1\) those happen to coincide, which hid the distinction. Here the common bound is \(-i/7\), reducing the honest two-disc chart from the deliberately weak 54-variable superset to 30 unknowns. The 54-variable run was stopped at 120 s after its basis queue grew past 39,000; I’m replacing it with the correct 30-variable system and will rerun the saturation.
