+## 7. `OPEN[DESCENT-ANCHOR]`: exactly where it bites
+
+**PROVED-HERE (arithmetic check).** The denominator in Definition 5.1 is
+
+```text
+n-M_2-1 = (12t+4)-(12t+1)-1 = 2 != 0.
+```
+
+Thus the Phi calculation is nonsingular. But the same equality places `M_2` two
+Laurent indices *before* Lemma 2.1's quadratic anchor. Nonzero denominator does not
+identify those coefficients.
+
+For `t=2`, in `tilde_eta=Q^{-1/20}`,
+
+```text
+P=tilde_eta^(-28)+sum_j p_j(gamma)tilde_eta^j,
+N=17.
+```
+
+The exact 4-tuple requires all earlier non-`4`-divisible `p_j` to vanish and
+`p_17 in k*`; Lemma then gives `p_j in k` for `j<19` and
+`deg_gamma p_19=2`. Between indices `-27` and `16` there are 33 earlier
+nonmultiples of `4`. Turning `p_17` and those 33 vanishings into polynomials in the
+30 chart variables requires the explicit truncated Laurent ring map. That map was not
+supplied by Lemma 2.1 and has not been proved here.
+
+**Logical effect.** The order-filtered chart is a necessary **superset**. If its
+`c!=0` saturation is empty, `t=2` is empty a fortiori and the anchor is unnecessary.
+If it is nonempty or times out, no solution can be promoted to `REPRESENTATIVE` until
+the 33 vanishings and `p_17!=0` are checked. This is precisely where
+`OPEN[DESCENT-ANCHOR]` bites.
+
+## 8. Typed verdict and OPEN accounting
+
+The final classification is inserted after §6 completes. The possible promotions are
+limited exactly as follows:
+
+- **PROVED-HERE:** Lemma/Newton support compatibility for all `t`; Phi radii; the
+  `(8)-(13)` evaluation; the `t=1` enlarged-chart `SATURATED-EMPTY` control.
+- **NOT PROVED:** theorem (T) for all `t`; existence of any ray pair; any lift back to
+  a Keller pair.
+- **OPEN[DESCENT-ANCHOR].** Bounded quantity at `t=2`: 33 pre-anchor nonmultiple
+  vanishings plus one nonzero `p_17`, obtained from a Laurent expansion through index
+  19. Cheapest test: implement the monic fractional-series map
+  `tilde_eta=Q^{-1/20}` in the declared coefficient ring, verify by recomposition,
+  and add a separate Rabinowitsch variable for `p_17`.
+- **OPEN[T-UNIFORM-COEFFICIENT].** Bounded at fixed `t` by `9t+12` ungauged unknowns.
+  Cheapest next test after `t=2`: exploit the three safe target gauges and the
+  banded `h`-adic identity before attempting a generic-`t` recurrence.
+
+**FALLACY-v2 audit.** No screen is called attainment. The formal Newton/characteristic
+compatibility is not a polynomial pair. The actual monomial-Jacobian control is not
+promoted into the 4-tuple. Saturation is by an explicit Rabinowitsch generator in a
+declared ring and has empty/nonempty wrapper controls. Monic `h`-division handles zero
+remainders and needs no vanished-leader branch. Prime marks on descended data are
+labels. No exit-price assertion is made, so no `charge_basis` line is due.
